is back toward a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Monica De La Cruz (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas's 15th District pairs first-term Republican incumbent Monica De La Cruz against Tejano singer Bobby Pulido, a well-funded Democratic recruit. The district leans Republican by about seven points, and the incumbent holds a cash advantage, but Pulido has raised nearly $3 million and drawn heavy media attention. Recent polls, including a September survey, show him leading by five to thirteen points, though several are Democratic-sponsored. Expert ratings split between Tossup, Lean R, and Lean D, reflecting genuine uncertainty about whether Republicans' 2024 gains with South Texas Latino voters will hold. Prediction markets, however, price Pulido around 82 percent, well above what the fundamentals alone would suggest. The race sits at the intersection of national House control and the battle over the Latino vote, making it one of the most closely watched Texas contests of the cycle.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4454, "margin": -0.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6234, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6548, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6308, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6942, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6077, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6479, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7065, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6601, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6541, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6766, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6611, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6572, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6619, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6805, "margin": 3.0}, {"date"